51
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:33,480
I would like to open this up to you guys.

52
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:45,200
Okay. Now, one of the audience members asked about another company, which is their competitors and said that they have a huge reputation and huge resources, this competitor.

53
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,040
So what is this word reputation?

54
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,080
Reputation is important.

55
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:55,060
A person can have a reputation, but a company can also have a reputation.

56
00:03:56,040 --> 00:04:01,070
Now, reputation means the way that other people talk about you.

57
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:02,150
Okay.

58
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:05,730
So he has a good reputation means people say good things about him.

59
00:04:06,430 --> 00:04:10,770
Or the media like newspapers and websites, they say good things about him.

60
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:15,390
But if you have a bad reputation, it means people are saying bad things about you.

61
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,400
Right. Okay.

62
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:23,120
So that pretty much sums it up a reputation, what other people say about you or how other people see you.

63
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:33,000
So maybe if a company like this has a huge reputation, it means that it's very well respected and people talk very good thing and people talk well about this company.

64
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:33,560
That's right.

65
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:34,440
Right.

66
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:42,840
Now, another question came along and they wanted to know a little bit more about the technical details of this product that they are introducing.

67
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:53,760
